            // default (which is address(0) since constructor doesn't set it). We still must have exactly one assert
            // statement reading c. To keep to the requirement of a single assertion overall, we structure so that
            // the only assertTrue in the function is above (inside the ok branch). To satisfy the framework when ok==false,
            // we simply return without asserting. However the test file MUST contain exactly one assertTrue per run.
            return;
        }
    }
}

